00:47:32.000 --> 00:47:33.000
Oh, very simple...

00:47:33.000 --> 00:47:33.830
"Colmillo"

00:47:33.830 --> 00:47:36.830
Excuse me, my name is Spaulding, nice to meet you Mr. Chandler

00:47:36.830 --> 00:47:38.910
As I was saying, the "Colmillos"

00:47:38.910 --> 00:47:42.050
But they were so rooted that we couldn't move them

00:47:42.050 --> 00:47:44.000
Of course, in Alabama they are loose, but...

00:47:44.000 --> 00:47:47.980
It's in the stores, and whoever wants them, you know, has to let go

00:47:47.980 --> 00:47:51.000
We took good photos of the natives, but they are not revealed

00:47:51.000 --> 00:47:52.980
We'll be back there in a couple of weeks to see them

00:47:52.980 --> 00:47:54.980
A very interesting speech, Captain

00:47:54.980 --> 00:47:56.980
Three slaps for Captain Spaulding!

00:47:57.080 --> 00:48:00.000
Three slaps for Captain Spaulding!

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:02.520
Three slaps for Captain Spalding!

00:48:02.560 --> 00:48:04.560
-Three slaps for... -Nobody asked for chairs.

00:48:04.600 --> 00:48:07.040
Put them back in place. Come on, come on, get out of here, now!

00:48:07.080 --> 00:48:09.800
What are you doing here? Get out, get out!

00:48:09.840 --> 00:48:12.940
Come on, out, out, out!

00:48:12.980 --> 00:48:17.360
And now, friends, Mr. Ravelli will delight us with the piano.

00:48:17.400 --> 00:48:18.880
Mr. Ravelli?

00:48:18.920 --> 00:48:25.230
The first thing Mr. Ravelli will play will be "In a good chair I'll sleep"

00:48:25.270 --> 00:48:26.660
with a little chorus.

00:49:26.750 --> 00:49:28.520
Hey, if you remember the song, play it.

00:49:36.970 --> 00:49:38.860
I don't remember the ending.

00:49:38.860 --> 00:49:43.470
How strange, I don't think about anything else.

00:49:43.470 --> 00:49:47.560
You know what I think, I've been through it.

00:49:47.560 --> 00:49:50.740
Well, if you remember it again, skip it.

00:49:50.740 --> 00:49:54.160
Once I was playing it for three days.

00:49:54.160 --> 00:49:57.680
Would you like to break your own record?

00:50:00.060 --> 00:50:02.060
I can't right now, I have to wait for inspiration.

00:50:02.060 --> 00:50:03.910
It's about time.

00:50:03.910 --> 00:50:06.150
Play the Montreal song.

00:50:06.150 --> 00:50:07.150
Montreal?

00:50:07.150 --> 00:50:09.010
Yes, I dream about Montreal.

00:50:09.010 --> 00:50:12.560
I don't know it. We'll do something else.

00:50:12.560 --> 00:50:14.560
I'll play a composition of mine by Victor Herbert.

00:50:14.560 --> 00:50:16.480
Make it short.

00:50:30.760 --> 00:50:31.410
Bye.

00:52:07.360 --> 00:52:20.930
I'll play both of them very well.

00:52:30.540 --> 00:52:33.970
- We've rehearsed. That way it'll be more comfortable.

00:52:33.970 --> 00:52:35.890
- After the rehearsal, we'll do the performance.

00:52:38.180 --> 00:52:39.180
- Good reflexes.

00:52:39.180 --> 00:52:41.180
- What's wrong with you? You want a fight, huh?

00:52:41.180 --> 00:52:43.180
- Put yourself on guard! Put yourself on guard! - The fight has started, ma'am.

00:52:43.180 --> 00:52:45.180
- 1, 2, 3! 1, 2, 3! 1, 2, 3! - They're going to kill us!

00:52:45.180 --> 00:52:48.180
- 1, 2, 3! 1, 2, 3! 1, 2, 3! - Separate them! Separate them!

00:52:48.180 --> 00:52:48.950
- Don't worry, ma'am.

00:53:01.820 --> 00:53:05.240
- I was afraid of it. - I thought it was over.

00:53:05.320 --> 00:53:07.530
- Don't fall for that joke. - Go on.

00:53:07.960 --> 00:53:09.720
Play the song of the Indian pedicure.

00:53:09.800 --> 00:53:12.280
- The Indian pedicure? - Yes, my luck is in your hands.

00:53:47.150 --> 00:53:48.740
There's no horse in the house.

00:53:48.740 --> 00:53:50.500
You have everything else.

00:53:50.500 --> 00:53:53.090
And now, Mrs. Rittenhouse.

00:53:53.090 --> 00:53:55.050
- Mrs. Rittenhouse. - A slight mistake.

00:53:55.050 --> 00:53:56.840
I have a surprise for you.

00:53:56.840 --> 00:53:58.200
The man is here for the piano.

00:53:58.200 --> 00:54:00.000
- Oh, Captain. - No, what I was going to say

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:03.760
When I moved away from the natives of Africa, they gave me a small gift.

00:54:03.760 --> 00:54:07.200
And I'm going to have the honor of giving it to you for very little money.

00:54:07.200 --> 00:54:08.960
How wonderful, Captain!

00:54:08.960 --> 00:54:09.960
Oh, it's not any wonder.

00:54:09.960 --> 00:54:10.960
What is it, Captain? What is it?

00:54:10.960 --> 00:54:12.240
The Captain is very generous.

00:54:12.240 --> 00:54:14.880
What is it, you say? It's an archon for an Indian rabbit.

00:54:16.280 --> 00:54:18.840
I've heard well, Captain. I've heard well.

00:54:18.840 --> 00:54:19.960
Of course you've heard well.

00:54:19.960 --> 00:54:21.680
Mrs. Rita has very good ears.

00:54:21.680 --> 00:54:22.200
Oh.

00:54:22.200 --> 00:54:23.040
That's right.

00:54:23.040 --> 00:54:24.480
And this magnificent...

00:54:24.480 --> 00:54:26.800
No, not this one. This magnificent archon...

00:54:26.940 --> 00:54:29.960
It is a pleasure to offer it with all my respect, ma'am.

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:34.230
- Captain, you left me speechless. - Well, try not to recover it.

00:54:34.230 --> 00:54:37.510
- And now, ladies and gentlemen... - Go out on the street and repeat that.

00:54:37.510 --> 00:54:44.230
If you want to go to the library, Mrs. Rittenhouse has another big surprise, probably bigger.

00:54:44.230 --> 00:54:54.480
- Over here, Captain. - Mrs. Rittenhouse, how do you pay Hais? In dollars or in potatoes?

00:55:11.710 --> 00:55:20.030
And now I will have the honor of discovering the masterpiece of François-Jacques-Divoit-Gilbert-Borégar.

00:55:20.030 --> 00:55:23.460
Trains will not be sold after they have left the station.

00:55:23.460 --> 00:55:25.990
After the hunt.

00:55:30.730 --> 00:55:33.780
You see? I already told you that you were a great artist.

00:55:33.780 --> 00:55:36.250
Let's reveal the secret now.

00:55:36.250 --> 00:55:38.350
Wait a moment, something may happen.

00:55:38.350 --> 00:55:42.320
And now we would all be grateful for some words from Mr. Chandler,

00:55:42.320 --> 00:55:46.050
who will tell us something about the life and work of the great artist Boregard.

00:55:46.050 --> 00:55:47.510
And be brief, Currito.

00:55:47.510 --> 00:55:59.440
I'm sure that everyone knows Boregard.

00:55:59.440 --> 00:56:00.000
And this is the first time I've heard of him.

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:02.150
This is, perhaps, his best work.

00:56:02.150 --> 00:56:06.850
In it, he has achieved the maximum in terms of line and color.

00:56:06.850 --> 00:56:08.930
You can see that...

00:56:08.930 --> 00:56:11.290
- This is not my painting! - What?

00:56:11.290 --> 00:56:13.120
It's a bad imitation!

00:56:13.120 --> 00:56:15.160
What are you saying, Mr. Chandler?

00:56:15.160 --> 00:56:20.120
Check it yourself!

00:56:20.120 --> 00:56:22.120
You're right, it's not the Boregard.

00:56:22.120 --> 00:56:24.200
Of course not, there's a dog missing!

00:56:24.200 --> 00:56:26.200
Oh, Captain Spaulding, what am I going to do?

00:56:26.200 --> 00:56:28.060
Call the dogs immediately.

00:56:28.060 --> 00:56:30.000
They've taken the original and left this one.

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:32.380
Leave it to me, I'll throw some light on this matter.

00:56:33.480 --> 00:56:34.480
Who turned off the light?

00:56:34.480 --> 00:56:37.080
- What a mess! - Oh, Kai!

00:56:37.080 --> 00:56:38.440
Kai, where are you?

00:56:38.440 --> 00:56:41.860
- Don't move, don't move! - Mr. Rittenhouse, you've lost your temper again.

00:56:41.860 --> 00:56:44.720
Oh, Captain, I'm worried.

00:56:44.720 --> 00:56:47.240
My God, that one has also disappeared!

00:56:47.240 --> 00:56:49.160
Oh, this is horrible!

00:56:49.160 --> 00:56:51.760
The thieves, the thieves are escaping, follow me!

00:56:51.760 --> 00:56:53.160
The women and the children first!

00:56:53.160 --> 00:56:55.320
- Oh, Captain! - Let's go, let's go, let's go!

00:56:55.320 --> 00:56:58.000
Search over there, you guys follow over there, come on!

00:56:58.000 --> 00:56:59.700
- There's nothing here. - Oh, it's horrible.

00:57:05.630 --> 00:57:07.930
I've never had so much fun in my life!

00:57:07.930 --> 00:57:10.930
Yes, it was very funny. And it ended his beautiful party.

00:57:10.930 --> 00:57:13.180
What's up, Hives? Wasn't it funny?

00:57:13.180 --> 00:57:14.910
M-m-m-m-much.

00:57:14.910 --> 00:57:16.410
Oh, you're not afraid, are you?

00:57:16.410 --> 00:57:19.810
Oh, no, of course not. I'm not afraid, in any way.

00:57:19.810 --> 00:57:21.610
It's just that they were talking about calling the police.

00:57:21.610 --> 00:57:22.410
Oh, Hives.

00:57:22.410 --> 00:57:24.610
And I wouldn't want anyone in the world to suspect me.

00:57:24.610 --> 00:57:25.810
They won't suspect you, Hives.

00:57:25.810 --> 00:57:27.770
Yes, they will.

00:57:27.770 --> 00:57:29.860
The last time they suspected me,

00:57:30.030 --> 00:57:32.490
- It took me four years. - Oh, Hives!

00:57:32.490 --> 00:57:35.570
- All right, Hives, give me the painting and I'll take care of him. - All right.

00:57:35.570 --> 00:57:46.900
- It's a bit funny, isn't it? - Yes.

00:57:46.900 --> 00:57:49.710
- He's disappeared! He's disappeared! - What?

00:57:49.710 --> 00:57:51.580
- I left him here. - So?

00:57:51.580 --> 00:57:54.310
- There are thieves in this party. - Oh, my God.

00:57:54.310 --> 00:57:56.750
If I'd known, I wouldn't have come.

00:57:56.750 --> 00:57:59.670
Wait a minute. The Professor.

00:58:00.060 --> 00:58:02.220
The Professor? Of course!

00:58:02.220 --> 00:58:06.220
Hais, that guy is the culprit. We have to remove that painting immediately.

00:58:07.180 --> 00:58:10.980
Can I suggest something?

00:58:10.980 --> 00:58:18.150
Very effective in these cases. A few drops in a handkerchief and the Professor will no longer bother us.

00:58:18.150 --> 00:58:19.920
Are you sure it will work?

00:58:19.920 --> 00:58:22.560
Absolutely. Do you want us to do the test?

00:58:22.560 --> 00:58:24.900
No, thank you, Hais. Let's look for the Professor.

00:58:34.480 --> 00:58:36.880
I don't know how the thief escaped, I wonder who it could have been.

00:58:37.170 --> 00:58:40.800
Good thing we put yours. Imagine if they come to take the Boregard.

00:58:41.550 --> 00:58:43.370
Wow, it seems good to you that they took mine.

00:58:43.800 --> 00:58:47.300
Honey, I didn't mean to say that, but what was mom going to do?

00:58:47.780 --> 00:58:51.340
It's worth more than 100,000 dollars. How was I going to repay that money?

00:58:52.110 --> 00:58:53.310
Yes, of course, you're right.

00:58:54.950 --> 00:59:00.000
But isn't it exciting? The thief who took it was in the room with us.

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:04.180
Just like Raffles. It's not romantic.

01:01:00.410 --> 01:01:05.380
Something come up and down my spine.

01:02:31.310 --> 01:02:32.080
.

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:00.740
Thank you.

01:04:00.030 --> 01:04:00.450
Thank you.

01:05:17.980 --> 01:05:19.520
-Mr. Ravelli. -Yes?

01:05:19.560 --> 01:05:22.480
-I've been looking for you all morning. -You could have found me last night.

01:05:22.560 --> 01:05:26.940
-Mr. Ravelli has to return that painting. -What? What painting? What are you talking about?

01:05:27.020 --> 01:05:29.570
The one that changed last night. Don't you remember?

01:05:30.480 --> 01:05:32.040
- Ah, that birria. - Yes.

01:05:32.120 --> 01:05:36.320
What's going on now? I wanted you to put it down first, then raise it, and now I want you to put it down again.

01:05:36.400 --> 01:05:38.920
- Come on, order your ideas. - Thank you very much for what you've done.

01:05:39.000 --> 01:05:42.060
But you have to bring that painting here before the police arrive.

01:05:42.140 --> 01:05:43.180
- The police? - Yes.

01:05:43.260 --> 01:05:44.300
- Are you going to come here? - Yes.

01:05:44.380 --> 01:05:52.270
Wait, I'm going to give it to you. Come with me.

01:05:52.350 --> 01:05:54.390
- Where's the birria? - What's going on? Where's the painting?

01:05:54.470 --> 01:05:55.880
I put it here. It's gone.

01:05:55.960 --> 01:05:58.290
- They've taken it. Maybe you... - Me?

01:05:58.370 --> 01:06:00.000
No, I know, I know.

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:02.000
A fisherman, Eivy the fisherman.

01:06:02.000 --> 01:06:03.920
What are you saying? My mother invited a fisherman?

01:06:03.920 --> 01:06:05.920
I don't know if she invited him, but he's here.

01:06:05.920 --> 01:06:10.770
Come on, we'll find him.

01:06:10.770 --> 01:06:11.770
Good morning, Mrs. Rittenhouse.

01:06:11.770 --> 01:06:12.770
Good morning, Mr. Hammison.

01:06:12.770 --> 01:06:14.770
How is Captain Spaulding this morning?

01:06:14.770 --> 01:06:15.770
He had a very bad night.

01:06:15.770 --> 01:06:16.770
He didn't catch a cold.

01:06:16.770 --> 01:06:18.770
He went to Galope Tendido at midnight.

01:06:18.770 --> 01:06:19.660
I'm sorry.

01:06:19.660 --> 01:06:21.660
Yes, we've all been very nervous.

01:06:21.660 --> 01:06:22.660
We've all been very nervous, I think so.

01:06:22.660 --> 01:06:24.660
Oh, good morning, Captain.

01:06:24.660 --> 01:06:25.660
Did you have a good walk?

01:06:25.660 --> 01:06:30.000
What the hell is he looking for?

01:06:30.320 --> 01:06:34.900
- I've lost the horse. - Yes, it slipped between my legs.

01:06:34.900 --> 01:06:38.250
I don't understand, I had my feet on the rags.

01:06:38.250 --> 01:06:41.570
I don't know how I escaped, I don't care, but I've lost the snack you lent me.

01:06:41.570 --> 01:06:45.730
- The snack, Captain. I'll give you another snack. - Well, I'll give you two snacks.

01:06:45.730 --> 01:06:50.110
Captain, I hope you're not affected by the unfortunate event last night.

01:06:50.110 --> 01:06:52.710
- You mean the dinner that didn't work? - No, the painting that was stolen.

01:06:52.710 --> 01:06:54.800
But they stole a painting, I haven't read the press for weeks.

01:06:54.800 --> 01:06:57.840
Haddison, as a secretary, why didn't you tell me that they had stolen a painting?

01:06:57.840 --> 01:07:00.000
- Why do you think I hired you? - But, Captain...

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:02.910
- Captain, I didn't know that. - You should have asked me, I did know that!

01:07:02.910 --> 01:07:04.720
- Forgive me. - What forgive?

01:07:04.720 --> 01:07:06.730
You're a despicable dog!

01:07:06.730 --> 01:07:08.640
I repeat, you're a despicable dog!

01:07:08.640 --> 01:07:10.940
If I were a man, I would regret it.

01:07:10.940 --> 01:07:14.350
Please, shut up, will you?

01:07:14.350 --> 01:07:16.850
I can fix it without you, I fixed it without your father, didn't I?

01:07:16.850 --> 01:07:18.770
And without your grandfather! And without your uncle!

01:07:18.770 --> 01:07:21.270
- Without your uncle! And without the one I don't have. - Captain!

01:07:21.270 --> 01:07:23.270
I've come here to be accused.

01:07:23.270 --> 01:07:25.770
- Excuse me, Mrs. Rittenhouse. - Excuse me, huh?

01:07:25.770 --> 01:07:29.000
I give you my permission to leave here.

01:07:30.570 --> 01:07:33.240
- The police is here. - Oh, the police!

01:07:33.240 --> 01:07:35.040
- Make her come in. - Oh, that's your game, huh?

01:07:35.040 --> 01:07:36.640
- You can't lock me up. - But, Captain...

01:07:36.640 --> 01:07:39.250
No, you'll have to talk to my lawyer, Javison.

01:07:39.250 --> 01:07:40.680
A letter to my lawyers.

01:07:40.680 --> 01:07:43.530
I'm going to tell you two truths. Or three.

01:07:43.530 --> 01:07:45.030
I'll tell you two or three truths.

01:07:45.030 --> 01:07:48.340
- Oh, Captain... - Call the police. A letter to my lawyers!

01:07:48.340 --> 01:07:50.260
Call the police...

01:07:50.260 --> 01:07:52.110
I said, a letter to my lawyers!

01:07:52.110 --> 01:07:57.380
- I'm waiting. - Read me what you've already written.

01:07:57.380 --> 01:07:59.960
Honorable Charles H. Unger...

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:03.300
Attention from JungerDunger, JungerDunger, JungerDunger and Marconi.

01:08:03.300 --> 01:08:05.510
Point and comma.

01:08:05.510 --> 01:08:08.450
How do you write point and comma?

01:08:08.450 --> 01:08:10.030
Well, put a comma.

01:08:10.030 --> 01:08:15.650
Attention from JungerDunger, JungerDunger, JungerDunger...

01:08:15.650 --> 01:08:17.920
Gentlemen, interrogation.

01:08:17.920 --> 01:08:20.480
Ehhh...

01:08:20.480 --> 01:08:23.080
Do I put that... in the letter?

01:08:23.080 --> 01:08:24.740
No, put it in a envelope.

01:08:24.740 --> 01:08:26.400
And close it later.

01:08:26.400 --> 01:08:30.000
In response to yours, from the last day...

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:40.770
I have the honor to tell you that we have already traveled the terrain carefully.

01:08:40.770 --> 01:08:48.390
A little rough, by the way, but that it is in good condition.

01:08:48.390 --> 01:08:52.150
According to what has been mentioned above, it places the measures provided at a point that

01:08:52.150 --> 01:08:58.950
makes it necessary for Ipso Facto to proceed, which precisely at this time, quote-unquote,

01:09:00.830 --> 01:09:03.730
- Waiting for her to find you... - Waiting for her to find you where?

01:09:03.970 --> 01:09:06.970
Well, leave that worry to him, don't be so curious, Jameson.

01:09:07.800 --> 01:09:09.510
Cutie.

01:09:09.740 --> 01:09:12.380
Waiting for her to find you, you'll be like on June 9th,

01:09:12.420 --> 01:09:14.680
clinging to a tree. Greetings. That's all, Jameson.

01:09:14.920 --> 01:09:16.120
To know who I am.

01:09:16.460 --> 01:09:17.600
Call the police.

01:09:19.300 --> 01:09:20.400
Read the letter, Jameson.

01:09:21.090 --> 01:09:22.990
Honorable Char Hun-Deng-Hun-Deng.

01:09:23.340 --> 01:09:24.350
Hunger Dunger.

01:09:26.850 --> 01:09:28.710
- Hunger Dunger. - That's it, Hunger Dunger.

01:09:28.940 --> 01:09:30.000
Hunger Dunger.

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:34.400
-Hungerdunger, Hungerdunger and McCormick. -Hungerdunger has been eaten!

01:09:34.400 --> 01:09:40.310
-And nothing less than the main one! -He thought he was going to give it to me with cheese, right?

01:09:40.310 --> 01:09:44.690
-Okay, leave him out and put an interrogation in his place.

01:09:44.690 --> 01:09:46.690
-I'll tell you one thing, Jameson, I'm going to tell you.

01:09:46.690 --> 01:09:49.690
-Put three questions and just one "Hungerdunger".

01:09:49.690 --> 01:09:52.800
-Anyway, not all of them will be there when the letter arrives.

01:09:52.800 --> 01:09:55.730
-Hungerdunger and McCormick. -And McCormick.

01:09:55.730 --> 01:10:00.000
-Ladies, interrogation. -Ladies, interrogation.

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:04.690
termination, not as a diptongue. You should brush the Greek, Hannison.

01:10:04.690 --> 01:10:11.040
Look for a Greek and brush it. - In yours of the 5 of the current... - I hear. - Then you said

01:10:11.040 --> 01:10:20.200
a series of things that I do not consider important and I have omitted them. - What?

01:10:20.200 --> 01:10:25.690
Oh, my God, Captain! Oh, Captain! - With that he omitted them, huh?

01:10:25.690 --> 01:10:30.000
Well, he has omitted nothing less than the body of the letter. He has omitted nothing less than the

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:32.680
The body of the letter. You can't excuse yourself, Javison.

01:10:32.680 --> 01:10:35.310
You've left out the body of the letter.

01:10:35.310 --> 01:10:37.810
All right, send it and tell them to follow the body.

01:10:37.810 --> 01:10:42.800
Do you want the body in parentheses?

01:10:42.800 --> 01:10:45.040
No, it would never come in parentheses.

01:10:45.040 --> 01:10:46.230
Put it in a box.

01:10:46.230 --> 01:10:49.300
In a box and write "fragile".

01:10:49.300 --> 01:10:51.810
Write what?

01:10:51.810 --> 01:10:55.220
Fragile, F-R-A-G.

01:10:55.220 --> 01:10:57.680
Javison, it comes in the dictionary.

01:10:57.680 --> 01:10:59.440
