01:25:09.960 --> 01:25:11.240
Don't you remember?

01:25:11.240 --> 01:25:15.350
No, but I do remember seeing you somewhere.

01:25:15.350 --> 01:25:18.680
I don't know where you saw me, but I'll move away in the future.

01:25:18.680 --> 01:25:21.320
Captain, it has come to me like lightning.

01:25:21.320 --> 01:25:23.740
That painting has not been stolen.

01:25:23.740 --> 01:25:24.900
Do you know what has happened?

01:25:24.900 --> 01:25:26.770
That it has disappeared, Captain.

01:25:26.770 --> 01:25:30.000
Yes, it has disappeared, and do you know what has made it disappear?

01:25:30.000 --> 01:25:32.840
He would never get it right. Do you know what made him disappear?

01:25:32.840 --> 01:25:33.720
The "polillas".

01:25:33.720 --> 01:25:35.580
The "polillas" have eaten him.

01:25:35.580 --> 01:25:36.580
"Polillas Zurdas".

01:25:36.580 --> 01:25:41.400
Get out of here.

01:25:41.400 --> 01:25:43.940
Get out of here or they'll come after me.

01:25:43.940 --> 01:25:45.780
"Polillas Zurdas eating pictures".

01:25:45.780 --> 01:25:47.400
Yes, it's the only solution.

01:25:47.400 --> 01:25:48.400
That's what I want to see.

01:25:48.400 --> 01:25:50.800
"Polillas Zurdas eating pictures".

01:25:50.800 --> 01:25:54.130
I'd buy him a parachute if I knew it wouldn't open.

01:25:55.130 --> 01:25:57.140
I already have a parachute.

01:25:59.140 --> 01:26:00.000
He's crazy.

01:26:00.350 --> 01:26:03.530
Come on, let's go down and ask for the reward. We have solved it, you have solved it.

01:26:03.530 --> 01:26:06.750
The painting has been devoured by blackmailers, all the credit is yours.

01:26:06.750 --> 01:26:08.910
- Do you know that we have done a good job? - How are you? Tired?

01:26:08.910 --> 01:26:11.030
- No, I'm not tired. - Where should you lie down for a couple of years?

01:26:11.030 --> 01:26:13.530
- I'm not sleepy yet. - Why don't you lie down until the rigor mortis arrives?

01:26:13.530 --> 01:26:15.950
- I'm not dead yet. - I'll tell you how we can recover the painting.

01:26:15.950 --> 01:26:19.430
We will go to the courts with a script of Habeas Corpus.

01:26:19.430 --> 01:26:24.040
- What do you want to write? - I shouldn't have started there, I understand.

01:26:24.040 --> 01:26:28.060
I say that we will go to the courts and we will get a script of Habeas Corpus.

01:26:28.060 --> 01:26:30.000
Yes, Scorpus, Scorpus. Have you seen the book?

01:26:30.030 --> 01:26:32.030
No, but I've seen valencian mermaids.

01:26:33.030 --> 01:26:34.850
You're crazy!

01:26:34.850 --> 01:26:36.800
Good morning.

01:26:36.800 --> 01:26:38.850
Good morning.

01:26:39.850 --> 01:26:44.250
Mr. Chandler, why don't you go down to the beach with the others?

01:26:44.250 --> 01:26:46.170
I'm sure it will fit you well.

01:26:46.170 --> 01:26:49.170
If I had my Boregard, it would fit me much better.

01:26:49.170 --> 01:26:51.170
We're doing everything we can.

01:26:51.170 --> 01:26:53.170
Mrs. Rittenhouse, Mrs. Rittenhouse!

01:26:53.170 --> 01:26:54.170
Oh, the Boregard!

01:26:54.170 --> 01:26:56.170
Oh, my Boregard!

01:26:56.170 --> 01:27:00.000
Wait, this is not my Boregard, it's a bad imitation of mine.

01:27:00.000 --> 01:27:04.000
- Where did you find it? - In Mr. Parker's room, ma'am.

01:27:04.000 --> 01:27:06.260
- Parker? - One thing is certain:

01:27:06.260 --> 01:27:09.180
the man who painted this stole the Boregard.

01:27:09.180 --> 01:27:12.220
- Hives, look for Mr. Parker and tell him to come here. - Yes, ma'am.

01:27:12.220 --> 01:27:15.170
One moment. My men will bring him. Bring Mr. Parker.

01:27:15.170 --> 01:27:19.530
- What's wrong with the painting? - Look, there's nothing more to see it once...

01:27:19.530 --> 01:27:26.600
to realize that it's a bad imitation.

01:27:44.560 --> 01:27:45.680
Mom, what's the matter?

01:27:45.680 --> 01:27:52.020
Mr. Parker, something very mysterious has happened, and I think you're the only one who can explain it.

01:27:52.020 --> 01:27:53.500
I'll be happy if I can do it.

01:27:53.500 --> 01:27:58.140
It's not a mystery. We found this in your room. What have you done with the real Borregard, huh?

01:27:58.140 --> 01:28:00.000
Come on, confess.

01:28:00.000 --> 01:28:02.000
- I think it would be convenient... - I have nothing to say.

01:28:02.000 --> 01:28:04.000
Except that I don't know where is Boregar.

01:28:04.000 --> 01:28:05.820
How have we found this in his room?

01:28:05.820 --> 01:28:07.320
Come on, better come with me.

01:28:07.320 --> 01:28:08.640
- He can't take it. - Look.

01:28:31.600 --> 01:28:36.250
This program is brought to you by the kindness of Bikinis David.

01:28:36.250 --> 01:28:43.950
Either wear the bikini upside down or there is no law of gravity.

01:28:43.950 --> 01:28:45.960
- And this is very serious. - My tie!

01:28:45.960 --> 01:28:48.630
Oh, Captain! What can we do?

01:28:48.630 --> 01:28:50.750
- They're going to stop John. - Who's going to stop John?

01:28:50.750 --> 01:28:52.790
- Me, Captain. - Oh, it's you, big John.

01:28:52.790 --> 01:28:56.140
Well, the first thing they teach in Scotland Yard is not to stop an innocent.

01:28:56.140 --> 01:28:57.340
- He's not an innocent. - Oh, no?

01:28:57.340 --> 01:29:00.000
- I have to stop him anyway. - Of course.

01:29:00.000 --> 01:29:01.480
No one will be left alone!

01:29:01.480 --> 01:29:03.010
They can't stop him!

01:29:03.010 --> 01:29:04.090
I stole it!

01:29:04.090 --> 01:29:06.090
- Arabella! - Don't listen to people, it was me!

01:29:06.090 --> 01:29:07.980
- You're both lying! - It was me!

01:29:07.980 --> 01:29:08.980
I did it with my ax!

01:29:08.980 --> 01:29:11.480
He's crazy, he's crazy! I confess it was me!

01:29:11.480 --> 01:29:13.030
Maybe it wasn't anyone!

01:29:13.030 --> 01:29:16.030
- Maybe there wasn't such a painting! - It's true, maybe there wasn't!

01:29:16.030 --> 01:29:18.030
- I saw the painting! - Enough of conversation!

01:29:18.030 --> 01:29:20.030
- Who stole that painting? - Me!

01:29:20.030 --> 01:29:22.030
Oh, holy hell!

01:29:22.030 --> 01:29:25.200
Was it you? Did you take it?

01:29:25.200 --> 01:29:26.200
Where is it?

01:29:26.200 --> 01:29:28.680
That's a horse!

01:29:31.020 --> 01:29:33.520
The Boregard! That's my Boregard!

01:29:33.520 --> 01:29:36.090
No, I'm wrong. That's not your Boregard.

01:29:36.090 --> 01:29:38.890
Don't be ridiculous. I paid $100,000 for this painting.

01:29:38.890 --> 01:29:40.990
I know what I'm buying. Look at the signature.

01:29:42.540 --> 01:29:44.740
- John Parker. - He painted it, didn't he?

01:29:44.740 --> 01:29:45.740
He changed it!

01:29:45.740 --> 01:29:53.510
This is my Boregard!

01:29:53.510 --> 01:29:55.500
It's the Boregard, I tell you!

01:29:55.500 --> 01:29:56.550
It's him!

01:29:56.550 --> 01:30:00.000
But that copy has the color, the depth,

01:30:00.090 --> 01:30:01.550
The soul of the Beauregard!

01:30:01.550 --> 01:30:04.720
Only an artist has been able to paint a painting like that.

01:30:04.720 --> 01:30:05.920
Oh, John!

01:30:05.920 --> 01:30:08.560
- Is it possible that you have painted it? - Yes, sir.

01:30:08.560 --> 01:30:11.030
You are a genius, young man! A genius!

01:30:11.030 --> 01:30:14.230
I order you to paint a portrait of me immediately!

01:30:14.230 --> 01:30:17.030
You'll have to wait until tomorrow, I'll be busy all day.

01:30:17.030 --> 01:30:20.770
Yes!

01:30:20.770 --> 01:30:22.350
You'll have to come with me, guys.

01:30:22.350 --> 01:30:23.840
Don't take him, agent.

01:30:23.840 --> 01:30:26.300
He's returned the painting.

01:30:26.300 --> 01:30:29.400
My name is Spaulding, I've always wanted to meet you.

01:30:29.400 --> 01:30:30.000
All right.

01:30:30.480 --> 01:30:33.780
I leave you free this time, but I want to give you a piece of advice.

01:30:33.780 --> 01:30:36.080
Do you know people who are very doubtful?

01:30:36.080 --> 01:30:37.900
Do you want to be a shameless person?

01:30:37.900 --> 01:30:41.080
Why don't you go to your house?

01:30:41.080 --> 01:30:42.520
She doesn't have a house.

01:30:42.520 --> 01:30:45.920
Go to your house for a few nights and stay there.

01:30:45.920 --> 01:30:49.410
Think about your poor mother.

01:30:49.410 --> 01:30:58.090
Poor thing, night after night after night,

01:30:58.090 --> 01:31:00.000
waiting to hear her footsteps.

01:31:00.000 --> 01:31:01.180
in the staircase.

01:31:01.180 --> 01:31:02.560
It doesn't have a staircase.

01:31:02.560 --> 01:31:05.860
And I see a little light shining.

01:31:05.860 --> 01:31:07.780
Shining in the window.

01:31:07.780 --> 01:31:09.920
No, sir, the gas company has cut it.

01:31:09.920 --> 01:31:12.640
What I'm telling you is for your own good.

01:31:12.640 --> 01:31:15.960
And if you listen to me,

01:31:15.960 --> 01:31:18.720
you won't have to regret it.

01:31:18.720 --> 01:31:24.550
This is going to be long.

01:31:24.550 --> 01:31:26.610
There's only one thing left.

01:31:26.610 --> 01:31:28.260
Oh!

01:31:30.510 --> 01:31:35.310
I don't understand why the coffee is so late. Where is the milk?

01:31:35.310 --> 01:31:40.780
Well, of course you surprise me. I also thought I had something else.

01:31:40.780 --> 01:31:47.970
It's useless to give you advice. Captain, this time I'm sorry, but I have to take it. Come on, come on! Come on!

01:31:47.970 --> 01:31:49.970
- No! - I'm going to the bathroom!

01:31:54.980 --> 01:32:00.000
- Hey, Samison, a letter to my lawyers! - No, no, no! I'm sorry, boss.

01:32:00.000 --> 01:32:04.000
What a wonder, what a wonder!

01:32:06.600 --> 01:32:13.890
Quick, save the fumigator! Let's get out of here before they wake up!

01:32:13.890 --> 01:32:15.890
Quickly! Let's go, let's go!
